---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Your Name"
  description="Student designer based in 【城市】, working on posters, short films and AI visual pipelines."
>
  <section class="page-head wrap">
    <h1 class="t-display">
      <span class="line-mask"><span style="--i:0">About—</span></span>
    </h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-grid">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm a student at 【学校】, studying 【专业】. I spend most of my time making
        posters, editing short films and pushing AI tools until they behave like a
        real production pipeline.
      </p>
      <p>
        I came to design from curiosity rather than a formal art background. That
        means I learned typography from looking, and tooling from breaking things.
        It also means I care a lot about <em>how</em> something is made, not only
        how it looks.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now I'm interested in one question: when generation becomes cheap,
        what is still expensive? My answer so far — taste, consistency, and the
        discipline to throw away 90% of the output.
      </p>

      <h3>What I can do</h3>
      <p>
        Poster &amp; layout design · short-form video editing · AI image generation
        pipelines (ComfyUI / Stable Diffusion) · basic front-end (HTML/CSS/JS).
      </p>

      <h3>Currently</h3>
      <p>Open to internships, collaborations and commissioned poster work.</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="about-aside" data-reveal style="--d:1">
      <div>
        <h4>Based in</h4>
        <p>【城市】, China</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Focus</h4>
        <p>Poster · Film · AI Visual</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Available for</h4>
        <p>Freelance &amp; internship</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>Contact</h4>
        <p><a class="link-u" href="mailto:hello@example.com" data-cursor="hover">hello@example.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</Base>
